{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1291060-technocrat-books","id":1291060,"title":"Technocrat books?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-02-23T03:26:18-08:00","id":1291060,"title":"Technocrat books?","content":"Im fascinated with the texhnocracy. I think it's pretty cool.<br /> <br /> I also need more books. <br /> <br /> 1. Any toys, devices, and wonders?<br /> 2. Their history<br /> 3. The thought of the rank and file","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T11:54:44-08:00","id":1291210,"title":"","content":"Guide to the Technocracy is good, but readers tend to gloss over the Technocracy's darker parts, like Processing and Room 101.<br /> <br /> The Revised Convention Books are solid for protagonist Technocrats. The original Convention Books, not so much, being written from the perspective of the Technocracy as villains.<br /> <br /> Sorcerers Crusade depicts their origins as the Order of Reason, and what they looked like then. The Order of Reason book provides an indepth look at the overall organisation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T12:31:06-08:00","id":1291221,"title":"","content":"There's a Technocracy book for M20 in the works isn't there?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T12:37:42-08:00","id":1291223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1291060-technocrat-books?p=1291210#post1291210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Revised Convention Books are solid for protagonist Technocrats. The original Convention Books, not so much, being written from the perspective of the Technocracy as villains.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's how I explain the situation with the Union in Revised Edition. You know how the People's Republic of China is having a problem with how it's youth has been raised on Communist propaganda, and now they actually believe in Marxist ideals the state has no intention to living up to regarding economic equality, workers' rights, etc?: <a href=\"https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/28/world/asia/china-maoists-xi-protests.html\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/28/w...-protests.html</a><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.npr.org/2018/11/21/669509554/in-china-the-communist-partys-latest-unlikely-target-young-marxists\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://media.npr.org/assets/img/2018/11/20/rts1xe40_wide-0dbcacda1ca089bab9351c137d491dedb7300004-s1400-c100.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.npr.org/2018/11/21/669509554/in-china-the-communist-partys-latest-unlikely-target-young-marxists\" target=\"_blank\"> In China, The Communist Party's Latest, Unlikely Target: Young Marxists </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.npr.org/2018/11/21/669509554/in-china-the-communist-partys-latest-unlikely-target-young-marxists\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.npr.org/2018/11/21/669509554/in-china-the-communist-partys-latest-unlikely-target-young-marxists </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Chinese authorities are cracking down on student activists, exposing a paradox between a state founded on Marxist principles and the young people it calls upon to carry them out. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> This is what's happening with the rank and file Technocrats in Revised Edition. Control has used lofty ideals as propaganda lies to justify itself and keep the rank and file in line. But with the Avatar Storm and Control being cut off, the rank &amp; file left on Earth are largely those who actually BELIEVE in those lofty ideals, and now they're in position to start making decisions for the Union!<br /> <br /> It doesn't turn the Union into good guys YET, but it does put them at a crossroads where player characters can be the ones to shape the outcome.<br /> <br /> Of course the Revised Void Engineers book reveals what happened to those old school Technocratic villains from the previous Convention Books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T09:00:23-08:00","id":1291542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1291060-technocrat-books#post1291060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Im fascinated with the texhnocracy. I think it's pretty cool.<br /> <br /> I also need more books.<br /> <br /> 1. Any toys, devices, and wonders?<br /> 2. Their history<br /> 3. The thought of the rank and file</div> </div> </div> </div>1. The Technomancers' Toybox has some stuff for the Technocracy in it. Also ...<br /> 2. The Order of Reason and Artificers' Handbook books for Mage: The Sorcerers' Crusade. [Also the Swashbucklers' Handbook.]<br /> 3. In the realm of non-fiction, Thomas Sowell's books, <i>A</i> <i>Conflict of Visions</i> and <i>The Vision of the Anointed</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 02-25-2019, 02:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T20:53:24-07:00","id":1299843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1291060-technocrat-books?p=1291542#post1291542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1. The Technomancers' Toybox has some stuff for the Technocracy in it. Also ...<br /> 2. The Order of Reason and Artificers' Handbook books for Mage: The Sorcerers' Crusade. [Also the Swashbucklers' Handbook.]<br /> 3. In the realm of non-fiction, Thomas Sowell's books, <i>A</i> <i>Conflict of Visions</i> and <i>The Vision of the Anointed</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Wait. <br /> <br /> Um.. I've been on SB. they say that there are 2 technocracies.<br /> <br /> one in the umbra, one on earth. <br /> <br /> The on on earth is kinda normal. <br /> <br /> The one in the umbra is insane, with von neumann swarms, full powered battleships and battlecruisers, and entire universes devoted to R&amp;D and stockpiles of weapons. <br /> <br /> So... where is that mentioned?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T21:00:02-07:00","id":1299845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1291060-technocrat-books?p=1299843#post1299843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait.<br /> <br /> Um.. I've been on SB. they say that there are 2 technocracies.<br /> <br /> one in the umbra, one on earth.<br /> <br /> The on on earth is kinda normal.<br /> <br /> The one in the umbra is insane, with von neumann swarms, full powered battleships and battlecruisers, and entire universes devoted to R&amp;D and stockpiles of weapons.<br /> <br /> So... where is that mentioned?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> SB is wrong. Threat Null is mentioned in Void Engineers Revised.. its.. Not anything close to that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T21:16:32-07:00","id":1299850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1291060-technocrat-books?p=1299845#post1299845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> SB is wrong. Threat Null is mentioned in Void Engineers Revised.. its.. Not anything close to that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh hey. Tell me more about threat null.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T01:17:30-07:00","id":1299879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1291060-technocrat-books?p=1299850#post1299850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh hey. Tell me more about threat null.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Much of the Off world assets went crazy because of the Avatar Storm cut them off from earth and thus.. they &quot;Void adapted&quot; into Straw Men of their various Conventions(sans the VE of course!) It allows you to have Revised Edition Technocrats fight 1e/2e Technocrats! But they don't have whole universes full of R&amp;D, they don't have Von Neuman Swarms Some may have battleships still but.. so does Earth Technocracy.<br /> <br /> Autocthonia MIGHT be fully dedicated to Research... or it might still be the Exalted Crossover Character.. its... something scary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T01:26:03-07:00","id":1299883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1291060-technocrat-books?p=1299879#post1299879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Much of the Off world assets went crazy because of the Avatar Storm cut them off from earth and thus.. they &quot;Void adapted&quot; into Straw Men of their various Conventions(sans the VE of course!) It allows you to have Revised Edition Technocrats fight 1e/2e Technocrats! But they don't have whole universes full of R&amp;D, they don't have Von Neuman Swarms Some may have battleships still but.. so does Earth Technocracy.<br /> <br /> Autocthonia MIGHT be fully dedicated to Research... or it might still be the Exalted Crossover Character.. its... something scary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, so 1e and 2e has the real crazy stuff in the technocracy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T01:48:13-07:00","id":1299887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1291060-technocrat-books?p=1299883#post1299883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, so 1e and 2e has the real crazy stuff in the technocracy?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> YEs and No? Nothing like SBs seems to present but it does have issues like not understanding space size(&quot;if you have a dyson's sphere why the fuck do you care about earth anymore?&quot;) and a lot of painful bits like Vacinations make your soul fall off...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T04:04:18-07:00","id":1299898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1291060-technocrat-books?p=1299887#post1299887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> YEs and No? Nothing like SBs seems to present but it does have issues like not understanding space size(&amp;quot;if you have a dyson's sphere why the fuck do you care about earth anymore?&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> and a lot of painful bits like Vacinations make your soul fall off...</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. They said it was because earth had humanity on it. Which meant that it was the most important. <br /> <br /> The technocracy wasn't after power. It was after the dominion of humanity. And that meant earth was important.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T08:06:00-07:00","id":1299956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1291060-technocrat-books?p=1291223#post1291223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Here's how I explain the situation with the Union in Revised Edition. You know how the People's Republic of China is having a problem with how it's youth has been raised on Communist propaganda, and now they actually believe in Marxist ideals the state has no intention to living up to regarding economic equality, workers' rights, etc?: <a href=\"https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/28/world/asia/china-maoists-xi-protests.html\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/28/w...-protests.html</a><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.npr.org/2018/11/21/669509554/in-china-the-communist-partys-latest-unlikely-target-young-marxists\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://media.npr.org/assets/img/2018/11/20/rts1xe40_wide-0dbcacda1ca089bab9351c137d491dedb7300004-s1400-c100.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.npr.org/2018/11/21/669509554/in-china-the-communist-partys-latest-unlikely-target-young-marxists\" target=\"_blank\"> In China, The Communist Party's Latest, Unlikely Target: Young Marxists </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.npr.org/2018/11/21/669509554/in-china-the-communist-partys-latest-unlikely-target-young-marxists\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.npr.org/2018/11/21/669509554/in-china-the-communist-partys-latest-unlikely-target-young-marxists </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Chinese authorities are cracking down on student activists, exposing a paradox between a state founded on Marxist principles and the young people it calls upon to carry them out. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> This is what's happening with the rank and file Technocrats in Revised Edition. Control has used lofty ideals as propaganda lies to justify itself and keep the rank and file in line. But with the Avatar Storm and Control being cut off, the rank &amp; file left on Earth are largely those who actually BELIEVE in those lofty ideals, and now they're in position to start making decisions for the Union!<br /> <br /> It doesn't turn the Union into good guys YET, but it does put them at a crossroads where player characters can be the ones to shape the outcome.<br /> <br /> Of course the Revised Void Engineers book reveals what happened to those old school Technocratic villains from the previous Convention Books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh.<br /> Huh.<br /> You have just kind of solved a problem I have been wrestling with about how a BNS style larp could have. a playable Technocracy. Thanks!<br /> <br /> I too second the Revised Convention Books. With the grain of salt that they, like most WoD splatbooks, are told from a subjective, internal perspective and not necessarily one hundred percent correct. But it will give you the icldea of what they think they are.<br /> <br /> You also may want to read the Q&amp;A in the M20 Book of Secrets. There are a few questions about why M20 did what it did with Technocrats and some interesting answers from the authors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T13:19:57-07:00","id":1300056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1291060-technocrat-books?p=1299898#post1299898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Huh. They said it was because earth had humanity on it. Which meant that it was the most important.<br /> <br /> The technocracy wasn't after power. It was after the dominion of humanity. And that meant earth was important.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The resources available of a dyson's sphere would be GREATER than the entire Solar system. Now.. all of it is INHABITABLE. If you can make a dyson's sphere and even begin to colonize it.... Earth becomes a litteral backwater... a Dyson's sphere would hold Quatrillions of people.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T00:37:05-07:00","id":1300212,"title":"","content":"But first, the Technocracy needs to bring the Dyson Sphere into Conventional Space; until it does, colonizing it requires special preparations or it becomes a quick road to Void Adaptation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T05:41:24-07:00","id":1300245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1291060-technocrat-books?p=1300212#post1300212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But first, the Technocracy needs to bring the Dyson Sphere into Conventional Space; until it does, colonizing it requires special preparations or it becomes a quick road to Void Adaptation.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That just leads to more questions about how they built it in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T06:13:26-07:00","id":1300260,"title":"","content":"The Dyson Sphere used to be a Technocratic Realm (The COP). That means that there was no risk of Void Adaptation until the Storm cut it's connections with Earth (and transformed it into a black hole in the process).<br /> <br /> There were rumors that the Technocracy didn't build the Sphere, however. If that's the case then it's possible (as a reasonable headcanon) that only a small portion of it was protected against the Void","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T06:44:00-07:00","id":1300270,"title":"","content":"There fact that it needs a connection to Earth to maintain any protection it has against Void Adaptation is enough of a reason for the VEs not to disregard Earth entirely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T19:57:30-07:00","id":1300454,"title":"","content":"Simply put Its impossible to defy conservation of energy in the technocratic paradigm. Any possibility of building a Dyson's sphere and running it from Earth energy is.. a joke.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T22:06:03-07:00","id":1300469,"title":"","content":"No; violating the conservation of energy is Vulgar, not impossible. And outside of Conventional Space, it isn't even Vulgar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T09:09:48-07:00","id":1300562,"title":"","content":"Personally, I really like the original convention books. They're much more overtly antagonistic than Revised, but I think they humanised the actual membership of the Technocracy really well.<br /> <br /> Book of Chantries also had two different Technocratic chantries which get referenced in later books which are kinda interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T18:45:56-07:00","id":1300723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1291060-technocrat-books?p=1300469#post1300469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No; violating the conservation of energy is Vulgar, not impossible. And outside of Conventional Space, it isn't even Vulgar.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, it violates their basic paradigmatic concepts to create something from nothing or to do loaves and fishes tricks.. it also probably violates game mechanics with the insane need for quint to make that much matter from &quot;nothing&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T21:46:03-07:00","id":1300761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1291060-technocrat-books?p=1300723#post1300723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, it violates their basic paradigmatic concepts to create something from nothing or to do loaves and fishes tricks.. it also probably violates game mechanics with the insane need for quint to make that much matter from \u201cnothing\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not giving the Void Engineers enough credit for innovation; and it <i>is</i> the Void Engineers were talking about here, not one of those pencil-pusher Syndics back on Earth. This is the Convention that deals with force fields, cloaking devices, reactionless drives, inertial dampers, tractor beams, faster-than-light propulsion, Wave Motion Guns, Zero-Point Energy, teleporters, matter replicators, laser swords, artificial gravity, anti-gravity, and all sorts of other things that violate physics as understood by the Masses. If there's a conservation law (or any other law of physics, for that matter) that's getting in their way, they'll find a loophole that lets them get around it. (Which, in gamespeak, means \u201cthey'll go Vulgar\u201d, except that it isn't Vulgar where they tend to operate. Their Earthside operatives can't get away with a fraction of what their off-Earth agents can do.)<br /> <br /> All that said, they didn't create the COP ex-nihilo. They also didn't create it by disassembling a couple of Jupiter-sized planets for the raw materials, which is more along the lines of how they <i>would</i> do it if they had to \u2014 not because they <i>can't</i> create matter out of \u201cnothing\u201d (they have matter replicators), but because it's <i>easier</i> to use existing matter than to make matter out of nothing. <br /> <br /> No, they <i>found</i> the COP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}